# -- Kiro workspace (server IP, SSH command, PEM key path, partnership strategy,
#    family medical information) --
# Was tracked in this public AGPL repo until 10 Aug 2026 (untracked via
# git rm --cached, then a full history rewrite via git filter-repo). This
# rule stops it being re-added by accident. NOTE: also re-added twice this
# session after being lost to an uncommitted-.gitignore mistake during that
# same rewrite -- if this comment reappears missing, check for the same cause
# before re-adding blind.
.kiro/

# -- Shango register bundle and correspondence (third parties, un-agreed disclosures) --
# Ishaan's register, its amendment log, the consent ledger, extracted PDFs and
# our own replies about defects on either side, before either party has agreed
# they are publishable. Contains named reviewers -- Ahmad Abby, Brad Wolfe,
# Mayur Agnihotri, Piotr Reder, Tim Zlomke, Hooman Parta, Ali Bagheri, Won Jung,
# Paul Knowles -- Mayur's consent outstanding, Piotr gets the named cut first.
data/shango-register-seq13/
data/shango-register-*.txt
data/shango-reconciliation-*.txt
Shango_Disagreement_Register*.pdf
Hardin_AI_reconciliation_*.pdf
data/reply-ishaan-*.md
data/register-merkle-construction-defects.md
data/email-ishaan-*.md

# -- NOT ignored, deliberately: data/spec-tbn-receipt-1.md --
# The frozen receipt construction specification MUST be committed and pushed.
# Its digest is bound into signed receipts, and section 0 states that the
# digest resolves from any clone or mirror without depending on Hardin
# remaining reachable. That claim is only true once it is actually in the
# public repo. Do not add it here.

# -- Client / prospect commercial material (third parties, public repo) --
# Angora Shipping is a named third party and PH2004 is somebody else's
# proprietary product. Requirement notes name their people, mailboxes, vessels
# and internal folder structure. Nothing here has publication consent.
data/requirement-ph2004-*.md
data/angora-*
data/ph2004-*

# -- WARNING: gitignore rules cannot un-track a file that is ALREADY tracked --
# .kiro/steering/server-info.md and .kiro/hooks/tbn-data-verify.kiro.hook were
# both tracked and published on origin/main until 10 Aug 2026. Same defect
# class as data/api_keys.json. Fixed via git rm --cached + a full history
# rewrite (git filter-repo) across all branches, force-pushed. History no
# longer contains any of: .kiro/steering/server-info.md,
# .kiro/hooks/tbn-data-verify.kiro.hook, data/api_keys.json,
# docs/TBN-Shango-Partnership-Agreement-v2.md, gen_ishaan_key.py. Verified via
# the GitHub API directly (contents endpoint returns 404 on all 3 branches for
# all 5 paths), not just local checks. This comment stays as a marker of what
# was done and why, in case anyone is tempted to re-add these files thinking
# the ignore rule alone is protection -- it is not, for a file already tracked.

# -- Signed partnership agreement (Ishaan/Shango), was tracked+public since 22 May --
# Full commercial terms: revenue split, non-compete, both signatures. Untracked
# on Burhan's go 9 Aug; his email is still ishaan@shango.io in this file's own
# text, so it stays out even after the address correction to team@shango.in.
docs/TBN-Shango-Partnership-Agreement-v2.md
gen_ishaan_key.py